# librest -- the RESTful web service client GNOME Online Accounts talks to its
# providers through. Packaged for GOA and nothing else today.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/rest/0.9/rest-0.9.1.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=9266a5c10ece383e193dfb7ffb07b509cc1f51521ab8dad76af96ed14212c2e3
SRC_DIR=rest-0.9.1

# BLFS LISTS make-ca AS **REQUIRED** FOR THIS PACKAGE AND IT IS NOT.
# meson_options.txt makes `ca_certificates` a boolean defaulting **false**;
# only when it is turned on does meson go looking for a CA bundle. And then,
# with `ca_certificates_path` empty, it PROBES THE BUILD MACHINE over three
# hardcoded locations (/etc/ssl/ca-bundle.pem, /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt,
# /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt) and error()s if none exists -- so turning it
# on would compile in a path chosen by whatever the builder image happened to
# contain. Finding 42's shape.
#
# Left at false, which is both the default and the right answer: TLS trust in
# this tree runs libsoup -> glib-networking -> gnutls -> p11-kit's trust module,
# which is where the anchors actually live. Stated rather than inherited because
# the book says otherwise.
#
# -Dgtk_doc=false. Defaults TRUE, and gi-docgen is not packaged -- BLFS notes it
# "is also provided as a meson subproject, which will be used if -D gtk_doc=false
# is not passed". Every recipe here inherits --wrap-mode=nodownload, so that
# subproject is a hard configure failure rather than a quiet vendored copy.
#
# -Dexamples=false and -Dtests=false: both default TRUE, and the examples pull
# libadwaita and gtksourceview5 for a demo application.
#
# -Dvapi=false already matches the default; stated because its neighbours in
# this wave do not default the same way and a reader should not have to check.
#
# -Dintrospection=true, stated rather than inherited: gobject-introspection is
# packaged, and the .gir is what GOA's own introspection consumes.
#
# -Dsoup2=false is the default here. geocode-glib, one wave earlier, defaults
# the same option TRUE -- same ecosystem, opposite default. Stated in both.
MESON_ARGS="-Dca_certificates=false \
-Dintrospection=true \
-Dvapi=false \
-Dexamples=false \
-Dtests=false \
-Dgtk_doc=false \
-Dsoup2=false"
